@startuml InventoryRuntimeFlow
title Runtime flow: pickup and item use
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #4A5268
  LifeLineBorderColor #4A5268
  LifeLineBackgroundColor #F7F7FB
  ParticipantBorderColor #4A5268
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #E9ECF5
}

actor "Player" as Player
participant "Pickup overlap callback" as Pickup
participant "HeroInputSystem" as InputSystem
participant "ItemsSystem" as ItemsSystem
participant "PickupSystem" as PickupSystem
participant "InventoryUtils" as Inventory
participant "ItemAction / ActionQueue" as ActionQueue
participant "ActionsSystem\n(last gameplay system)" as ActionsSystem
participant "Observers / UI" as Observers

== Picking up an item ==
Player -> Pickup: enter pickup Area2D
Pickup -> Pickup: add C_PickedUp + OwnedBy(hero)
note over PickupSystem
  The tags make the pickup match PickupSystem
  during the next gameplay processing pass.
end note
PickupSystem -> PickupSystem: query C_IsPickup + C_PickedUp + OwnedBy(Hero)
PickupSystem -> ActionQueue: dispatch optional pickup action
PickupSystem -> PickupSystem: queue atomic inventory-add closure, then pickup removal
note over PickupSystem,Inventory
  The command-buffer flush runs the closure before removing
  the pickup, while its item template is still available.
end note
PickupSystem -> Inventory: at flush: add_to_inventory(hero, template, quantity)
Inventory -> Inventory: compose item entity; add OwnedBy(hero)
Inventory -> Inventory: consolidate matching type_id stacks
Inventory -> Observers: emit inventory_changed / active_item_changed
PickupSystem -> PickupSystem: remove floor pickup at flush
Observers -> Observers: rebuild quick bar from inventory query

== Using the active item ==
Player -> ItemsSystem: press use_item
ItemsSystem -> ItemsSystem: queue C_RequestUseItem on active item
note over ItemsSystem
  The use-input sub-system runs after the request
  consumer, so this request is intentionally honored
  on the following gameplay frame.
end note
ItemsSystem -> ItemsSystem: next frame: consume request and dispatch action
ItemsSystem -> ActionQueue: enqueue item action
ActionsSystem -> ActionQueue: drain at end of gameplay group
ActionQueue -> Inventory: action applies gameplay/inventory changes
Inventory -> Observers: emit event or component change
Observers -> Observers: update quick bar, status, toast, or door

@enduml
